From: Christopher Hotchkiss <christopher.hotchkiss@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 18:48:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] =?UTF-8?q?P8:=20macOS=20surface-embed=20=E2=80=94=20p?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ublish=20render=20CAMetalLayer=20via=20CAContext=20for=20CALaye?=
 =?UTF-8?q?rHost=20(SURFACE)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Combines the P8 series (was P8 + P8-v2 + the 720p follow-up) into one patch.

macOS analogue of P2's window-handle publish: instead of choreographing a
second top-level game window, the emulator hands its render layer to the
launcher, which hosts it INSIDE its own egui window via the private
CALayerHost / CARemoteLayer SPI.

- Dedicated off-view CAMetalLayer (surface_publish.mm): MoltenVK renders into a
  standalone layer (NOT the gs_frame NSView's backing layer — an already-attached
  backing layer won't also serialize through a CAContext), published via a private
  CAContext. The contextId is read over IPC by the SURFACE command.
- Window hidden (gs_frame.cpp show() suppressed under SKYLANDER_BORDERLESS): there
  is no on-screen game window; the launcher owns the frame.
- FIXED 16:9 720p render extent: gs_frame::client_width/height pinned to 1280x720
  under SKYLANDER_BORDERLESS, and the layer drawableSize sized to match. RPCS3 uses
  client_width/height for BOTH the swapchain extent AND the present blit target; the
  near-fullscreen window self-resizes during boot, which would otherwise shrink the
  blit target without recreating the swapchain (game rendered into a top-left
  sub-rect, black elsewhere). Pinning keeps swapchain == present == published layer,
  all 16:9 at the PS3's native 720p — one clean resample on the launcher side.
- SURFACE reply carries the surface size (OK context=<dec> size=<w>x<h>) so the
  launcher scales the hosted layer to its pane (CALayerHost renders the remote tree
  at native size; it does not auto-fit the host bounds).

Tested from Rust via the loopback (proto codec + ipc_loopback SURFACE round-trip);
live-validated on macOS (M3 Max) — Skylanders Giants composites in the launcher
window, filling the pane at 720p with a starfield-navy letterbox.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
